---
source: crates/ostro/tests/cli_p11.rs
expression: "help(&[\"dlq\", \"requeue\"])"
---
Requeue an entry: resume in place, restart with the same input, or rerun from a cut

Usage: ostro dlq requeue [OPTIONS] <RUN>

Arguments:
  <RUN>
          DLQ member (run id)

Options:
      --mode <MODE>
          How to requeue

          Possible values:
          - auto:    Resume when the run is resumable, else restart (server default)
          - resume:  Resume the run in place
          - restart: Start a new run with the same input
          - rerun:   Rerun from a cut (`--from-step` / `--from-seq`)
          
          [default: auto]

      --from-step <NAME[#N]>
          Cut before the N-th (1-based, default 1) execution of step NAME: `NAME` or `NAME#N`

      --from-seq <N>
          Cut at journal sequence number N (events before N are copied)

      --dry-run
          Validate only: report the mode that would be used, requeue nothing

      --server <SERVER>
          Server URL
          
          [env: OSTRO_SERVER=]
          [default: http://127.0.0.1:7700]

      --json
          Print the REST response body as JSON

      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Per-request timeout (friendly duration; a long-poll adds its wait)
          
          [default: 30s]

      --ca-file <PEM>
          PEM CA certificate to trust for an https:// server instead of the platform roots (e.g. the cluster CA `<data_dir>/tls/ca.crt` behind a self-signed listener)
          
          [env: OSTRO_CA_FILE=]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
